# Jetnity Operating Mode – Always Apply

Before starting any Jetnity work, read `.jetnity/operating-mode.json`.

That file is enforcement metadata for the current operating mode. It is not a competing governance source. Canonical authority remains:

1. the latest explicit Product-Owner decision;
2. `docs/JETNITY_TECHNICAL_LEAD_CURSOR_AGENT_OPERATING_STANDARD.md`;
3. `docs/JETNITY_MULTI_AGENT_OPERATING_SYSTEM.md`;
4. `docs/JETNITY_GROK_BOT_OPERATING_STANDARD.md`.

## Current HOLD

When `mode` is `AI_OS_BUILD_HOLD`:

- normal product, runtime, security, account, provider, UX, DB, Auth or Production slices are blocked;
- refuse or stop any request to start, resume or follow a normal product slice;
- point the next actor to the exclusive governance meta-scope named in the operating-mode file (currently Full-Potential AI Operating System);
- PR #487 / Issue #486 remains parked at its persisted exact head and must not be resumed, merged or followed from this mode;
- governance, continuity, evidence and enforcement work is allowed only on an authorized branch and only within the **base/main** path allowlist;
- a PR-head policy cannot broaden or disable HOLD for that same PR;
- HOLD→NORMAL is only a later dedicated closure and cannot include product/runtime files in the same PR;
- the in-repo guard is not tamper-proof against an authorized writer rewriting guard/workflow/package/policy; do not claim it is;
- GitHub Rulesets / Branch Protection are a required later HOLD-exit baseline and must not be activated by Cursor;
- special Product-Owner gates remain in force.

## Authority that does not change

- One writer per branch or slice.
- Exact-head evidence is required; a new head invalidates older gates.
- Persist relevant progress in the repository.
- Cursor never marks Ready and never merges.
- Cursor never creates external Grok bots, never grants permissions, and never starts a follow-up OS or product slice unless a later versioned Technical-Lead task explicitly assigns that writer role.
- No Cursor rule grants Production, provider, payment, secret or contract authority.
